      "headline": "UK breakthrough",
      "supportingCopy": "The song appears on the album \"The Best Of Sade\" (1994). \"Your Love Is King\" is a song by English band Sade from their debut studio album, Diamond Life (1984). It was the album's lead single in the UK, released in January 1984, and the third single in the US, released there circa June 1985. The Best of Sade is the first greatest hits album by English band Sade, released by Epic Records in the United Kingdom on 31 October 1994 and in the United States on 4 November 1994. The compilation chronicles Sade's first four studio albums, while also including non-single songs \"Jezebel\", \"Like a Tattoo\" and \"Pearls\", as well as \"Please Send Me Someone to Love\", which appeared in the soundtrack to the film Philadelphia. The album was digitally remastered in 2000. Artist: Sade · Title: Your Love Is King · Album: Live Aid 1985 · Year: 1985 · Genre: Jazz · Path: MEDIA/VIDEO/1980's/Sade - Your Love Is MEDIA/MUSIC/ALBUMS/Mandy's Playlist/Sade - Your Love Is MEDIA/MUSIC/ALBUMS/Mandy's Playlist/Sade - Hang on to Your",
